.TH "CLIPHIST-DAEMON.SH" "1" "November 2026" "arran4/dotfiles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cliphist\-daemon.sh \- manage clipboard watchers for a Hyprland instance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBcliphist\-daemon.sh\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Start wl\-paste clipboard watchers feeding cliphist. Use an instance\-specific lock and PID directory under XDG_RUNTIME_DIR (with a per\-user /tmp fallback), and restart only watchers matching the expected executable path. Typically launched by desktop configuration rather than interactively.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBHYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE\fR
Scopes the managed watcher processes; defaults to default outside Hyprland.
.TP
\fBXDG_RUNTIME_DIR\fR
Preferred directory for per\-instance PID and lock state.
.SH SEE ALSO
hyprland\-keys(7)
